    "body": "Adds a config for [nlpplus-language-server](https://www.npmjs.com/package/nlpplus-language-server), the language server for [NLP++](https://visualtext.org/nlp/), a programming language for natural language processing (open source, MIT).\n\n**Evidence for the new-config criteria**\n- **Popularity:** the server repo itself has fewer than 100 stars. It is the server behind the VisualText extension for VS Code ([dehilster.nlp](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=dehilster.nlp)), which has 10,804 Marketplace downloads (6,471 installs) and a 5.0 rating. The npm package is that same server, packaged for other editors.\n- **Active user base:** NLP++ has been in use since 1998:\n  - a [textbook](https://book.visualtext.org)\n  - a [Rosetta Code category](https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Category:NLP%2B%2B)\n  - [PLDB](https://pldb.io/concepts/nlp-plus-plus.html)\n  - a [LINGUIST List announcement](https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/2227/) (2026)\n  - a community forum ([nlp.discourse.group](https://nlp.discourse.group))\n  - HPCC Systems integration\n  - a Python package ([NLPPlus](https://pypi.org/project/NLPPlus/))\n\n**Notes**\n- Neovim doesn't detect `.nlp` files yet. vim/vim#21480 adds that, and the doc comment shows the one-line `vim.filetype.add` until it lands.\n- `spec` is the folder every NLP++ analyzer keeps its passes in, so it marks the project root.\n- Tested on Neovim 0.11.4 (Windows) with this repo on the runtimepath: `vim.lsp.enable('nlpplus_ls')` attaches to an analyzer and answers hover and workspace symbols, using the server installed by Mason (mason-org/mason-registry#17377). StyLua passes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
